id: gauge
name: Gauge
prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Clairvoyance
requiresSkill: clairvoyance
requiresRanks: 2
# "Session Limit: Infinite."
sessionLimit: infinite
timeCost: 1 Minute
# "Target a Character you can sense. Make a Clash (Clairvoyance vs Concealment) against them."
clashSkill: clairvoyance
clashDefenderSkills: concealment
# "You cannot target the same Character twice with the Gauge Maneuver in an Adventuring Session."
oncePerTarget: true
# "If you win, you learn their Power Level and Alignment."
clashReveals: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A Clairvoyance Clash against someone's Concealment: win, and you learn their Power Level and
  Alignment. Once for each Character in an Adventuring Session.
text: >
  Gauge: Using your ability to sense energy, you size up a potential threat, learning their relative
  strength compared to your own.
  –Prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Clairvoyance
  –Session Limit: Infinite
  –Time Cost: 1 Minute
  –Effect: Target a Character you can sense. Make a Clash (Clairvoyance vs Concealment) against them.
  If you win, you learn their Power Level and Alignment. You cannot target the same Character twice
  with the Gauge Maneuver in an Adventuring Session.

---

# Offered on the Adventure tab to whoever has 2+ Ranks in Clairvoyance, with no Session Limit. Used at
# the one token targeted - refused if they were already Gauged this Adventuring Session - and the
# Clash card opens at once. Won, their Power Level and Alignment are whispered to the one who Gauged
# them (and the GM). Whether they can be sensed is the table's.
